# reflect.StructOf gives a struct embedding a type with methods (a lone embedded field, as yaegi
# builds `type stamp struct{ time.Time }`) the promoted methods, and registers their code addresses
# with the runtime (resolveReflectText), which keeps them in maps of unsafe.Pointer: memory the
# garbage collector scans at every cycle. For the same reason as in reflect-code-pointers.patch, a
# code address is a heap pointer to the collector on wasm once the heap has grown past it. Code
# addresses are registered apart instead, as uintptr, from the same sequence of offsets, and textOff
# resolves them from there.

